Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||11-15-2001||10:25 PM||||what technique did you use to get yellow? I've never been able to make a dark car look yellow and have it even remotely realistic before...<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000012||MinnGreenGT||11-15-2001||10:32 PM||||That's not exactly a quick question/answer.  Basically I copied the layer (original on bottom), then adjusted the hue/saturation of the top image of the car until it was close to yellow (it was still pretty dark)- I OK'd that change.  Then I went back into the Hue/Saturation control and tweaked the remaining green to appear more yellow, as well as increasing the yellow saturation more.  On top of that, I also added another layer of yellow and adjusted it's opacity.  Then, on both of those layers I erased everything that wasn't supposed to be adjusted (background, tires, interior, etc...).  And finally I added one more layer and painted in the black trim and door splits- they had disappeared in the yellowing process.<P>I know this is kinda lenghty and still quite simplified... It's quite a bit of fartin' around- many hours in PhotoShop over the past 5 or 6 years.||||reg||1
